From e968b507eb9e2e6808deb733fb062b49c6e74ec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Garcia <44309076+ElGuslml@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:43:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] gpu: add a switch to turn host rendering off (sync-only
 command processor)

A renderer that draws the guest's frames from another source than the
command buffer (XenosNative, which hooks the game's XDK Direct3D library)
still needs the command processor for everything the game waits on:
fences, interrupts, swaps, event writes. It does not need the host draws,
which would only cost GPU time and present a frame nobody sees.

IGraphicsSystem::SetHostRendering(enabled) turns host rendering off (and
on again; it may be called at any time, for A/B comparisons). Off, the
command processor executes every packet as before, but:
- draws are not issued on the host, which also skips clears and resolves
  (resolves are copy-mode draws on Xenos);
- occlusion queries take the generic path that reports the fake sample
  count (query_occlusion_fake_sample_count), since no host draw counts
  samples.

The draw observer still sees every draw packet, with issued = false.
kGpuPluginAbiVersion is bumped for the new virtual function.

This patch is only for projects that use XenosNative; it is kept in
xenos_native/sdk_patches/ and applied after the shared series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
